{
  "format": 1,
  "name": "commercial_loaded_grids",
  "spec": ["commercial-industrial 4.4", "commercial-industrial 13.6"],
  "description": "The rebuild runs on the proximity grid itself (no temporary): a grid holding 9 at (4, 4) and 0 elsewhere off the edge holds 1 at (4, 4) afterwards (lowered to its neighbours + 1); a 0 at (2, 0) becomes 1 when map (2, 0) is not the key (the seed writes 255 there first). Values off the edge are only lowered: on a grid of all 9 the edge settles at 10 and every other cell keeps 9. Without a building map helper 0x005E5130 returns at once (CM5): no seed and no passes, so a loaded grid keeps every value (9 at (4, 4), 200 at (2, 0)), the previous result is kept, and a fresh grid stays all 0; the state machine still advances.",
